WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.900
Around 1970, Martin Rodbell's laboratory studied how glucagon switches on

2
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.480
adenylyl cyclase in liver membranes.

3
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.840
In plain buffer, the hormone stuck to the membranes and would not wash off.

4
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.680
Add ATP, and it came off within seconds.

5
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.560
That was odd, since ATP is the enzyme's fuel.

6
00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:32.053
The cause was a contaminant: commercial ATP carries a little GTP.

7
00:00:32.953 --> 00:00:36.173
Added on purpose, GTP proved to be required.

8
00:00:36.773 --> 00:00:40.033
Without it, glucagon barely switched the cyclase on.

9
00:00:40.953 --> 00:00:42.613
GTP was not the fuel.

10
00:00:43.193 --> 00:00:46.933
A trace was enough, so GTP was used over and over.

11
00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:53.887
For years almost no other laboratory could reproduce this, because most were not

12
00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:56.727
working with membranes as clean as Rodbell's.

13
00:00:57.347 --> 00:01:00.507
Suppose the ATP is 1% GTP.

14
00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:06.987
Then the tube with no GTP added already holds enough for a full response, so the

15
00:01:06.987 --> 00:01:08.927
difference between tubes never appears.

16
00:01:09.947 --> 00:01:15.347
Many receptors switch on the same enzyme, and Rodbell thought it impossible that all

17
00:01:15.347 --> 00:01:16.287
were built into it.

18
00:01:16.287 --> 00:01:20.807
So he proposed a separate component between them, a transducer.

19
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.400
The answer came from Alfred Gilman's laboratory at the University of Virginia.

20
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.860
Gilman and Elliott Ross used cyc⁻ lymphoma cells, where the link between

21
00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.800
receptor and enzyme is missing.

22
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.000
They added an extract from normal cells.

23
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:43.420
The response came back, even when the extract's own cyclase was inactivated.

24
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.620
So the transducer was a separate, movable protein.
